WEBVTT

00:00.360 --> 00:01.410
Instructor: Alright, so it's time

00:01.410 --> 00:03.840
for a quick exercise that just tests your ability

00:03.840 --> 00:05.700
to work with the git Stash command,

00:05.700 --> 00:07.650
and just in the most basic way.

00:07.650 --> 00:09.810
So we talked a lot or we talked about

00:09.810 --> 00:12.690
quite a few different variants of git stash.

00:12.690 --> 00:14.520
This exercise is really just the basics.

00:14.520 --> 00:16.740
Can you put something in it and take something out?

00:16.740 --> 00:17.573
Okay?

00:17.573 --> 00:22.053
So the premise here is that you're keeping a diary,

00:23.540 --> 00:25.800
and you're working in an office

00:25.800 --> 00:28.170
and your boss walks by and you need to

00:28.170 --> 00:32.040
quickly stash some changes before your boss sees them.

00:32.040 --> 00:35.160
So as always, you can find the link to this,

00:35.160 --> 00:37.050
this document as a resource.

00:37.050 --> 00:38.280
With this video, I recommend

00:38.280 --> 00:41.280
that you stop the video and try this on your own.

00:41.280 --> 00:45.000
Basically, you'll make a new repo, make a file called diary,

00:45.000 --> 00:47.130
and then inside of it write a sentence

00:47.130 --> 00:48.570
that says, "I love my boss".

00:48.570 --> 00:52.080
Save, add, and commit and that will be on the master branch.

00:52.080 --> 00:55.140
But then you make a new branch called "the truth"

00:55.140 --> 00:56.460
and you work on that branch.

00:56.460 --> 00:59.700
You switch to it and you erase the contents of the file,

00:59.700 --> 01:03.060
and you replace it with all of this, and you save the file.

01:03.060 --> 01:06.600
And just before you're able to add and commit,

01:06.600 --> 01:08.370
your boss walks towards you.

01:08.370 --> 01:09.780
You see them walking towards you,

01:09.780 --> 01:12.390
so you quickly switch over to the master branch.

01:12.390 --> 01:15.030
So that tells you, switch to master

01:15.030 --> 01:16.200
without adding and committing.

01:16.200 --> 01:18.660
So we switch over and oh no,

01:18.660 --> 01:22.530
the diary file still contains our truthful confession.

01:22.530 --> 01:25.860
Quickly stash the changes before your boss sees.

01:25.860 --> 01:28.147
So now the diary file should go back to just saying,

01:28.147 --> 01:29.730
"I love my boss".

01:29.730 --> 01:31.080
And the boss walks by.

01:31.080 --> 01:32.700
We add some more lies,

01:32.700 --> 01:35.310
just more lines that say I love my boss.

01:35.310 --> 01:38.100
Then we add and commit those changes on the master branch.

01:38.100 --> 01:39.210
Then our boss leaves.

01:39.210 --> 01:42.240
So we go back to the truth branch, we retrieve the changes

01:42.240 --> 01:44.550
from the stash, all of this.

01:44.550 --> 01:46.740
And then we add and commit on the truth branch

01:46.740 --> 01:47.850
and we're done.

01:47.850 --> 01:49.560
Okay, very simple.

01:49.560 --> 01:50.393
So let's try it.

01:50.393 --> 01:53.220
I recommend you do it on your own as always, but here we go.

01:53.220 --> 01:54.526
I'll do it.

01:54.526 --> 01:57.060
So we'll make a new repo in some folder.

01:57.060 --> 02:02.060
LS, let's make a folder called Stash-Diary.

02:03.780 --> 02:05.520
We'll cd into that.

02:05.520 --> 02:06.960
Make sure we're not in a repo.

02:06.960 --> 02:09.000
I'll git init and then I'm gonna make

02:09.000 --> 02:13.080
the diary.txt file and then I'll open that.

02:13.080 --> 02:15.960
Okay, so here's the file and I'm just gonna put

02:15.960 --> 02:19.080
I love my boss, I think is what it was.

02:19.080 --> 02:21.090
Yeah, you don't have to get it exactly right.

02:21.090 --> 02:23.310
And then we're going to add and commit.

02:23.310 --> 02:26.670
So add that diary file and then just a simple commit,

02:26.670 --> 02:27.963
add diary file.

02:29.580 --> 02:33.240
Okay, so then we create a new branch called the truth.

02:33.240 --> 02:34.740
We're gonna switch over to that.

02:34.740 --> 02:39.120
So git switch -c, the -truth.

02:39.120 --> 02:41.790
So I'm now on that branch, right?

02:41.790 --> 02:45.270
And I'm going to write the truth in this file.

02:45.270 --> 02:47.220
I hate my boss.

02:47.220 --> 02:50.040
And then I'll duplicate that four times or so.

02:50.040 --> 02:50.880
It doesn't matter.

02:50.880 --> 02:53.880
As long as we have some number of some lines in there

02:53.880 --> 02:55.320
some changes.

02:55.320 --> 02:58.020
And it's pretty obvious to see I have changed that.

02:58.020 --> 03:00.210
So I hate my boss, I hate my boss, I hate my boss.

03:00.210 --> 03:01.043
Okay.

03:01.043 --> 03:03.210
Oh, and just as a quick quiz,

03:03.210 --> 03:07.230
what is the command I could run to see what I've changed?

03:07.230 --> 03:10.110
Since we made this branch, right since the last commit.

03:10.110 --> 03:12.990
Well, there's a couple, but I could just do git diff HEAD.

03:12.990 --> 03:13.830
And there we are.

03:13.830 --> 03:15.240
We see that I removed this line

03:15.240 --> 03:17.130
and I added these lines in.

03:17.130 --> 03:21.480
Okay, so the next step I'm about to add and commit

03:21.480 --> 03:23.640
but oh no, my boss is walking towards us.

03:23.640 --> 03:26.670
Shoot, I gotta switch over to the master branch.

03:26.670 --> 03:29.040
Git switch back to master.

03:29.040 --> 03:31.380
Oh no, my changes came with me.

03:31.380 --> 03:32.490
This is a nightmare.

03:32.490 --> 03:33.960
My boss is about to see.

03:33.960 --> 03:36.240
Quickly, stash the changes.

03:36.240 --> 03:37.950
So I can do git stash,

03:37.950 --> 03:39.750
or git stash save.

03:39.750 --> 03:42.301
They're the same thing, it's just a shortcut.

03:42.301 --> 03:43.260
(Instructors gasps)

03:43.260 --> 03:46.950
Now my boss walks by and as they're walking by

03:46.950 --> 03:49.110
I just continue to write some more lies.

03:49.110 --> 03:51.240
I love my boss, I love my boss.

03:51.240 --> 03:54.900
I save, I'm even gonna add and commit these changes.

03:54.900 --> 03:59.900
Git add diary, git commit -m, add more lies.

04:01.350 --> 04:04.950
All right, so I'm now ready to switch back over

04:04.950 --> 04:07.260
because my boss has left the room.

04:07.260 --> 04:10.200
I can go back to the truth branch.

04:10.200 --> 04:15.200
Git switch the-truth, and we don't see my work, right?

04:16.230 --> 04:19.170
We don't see the, I hate my boss times five of course

04:19.170 --> 04:20.790
because it's in the stash.

04:20.790 --> 04:22.680
So how do I apply those changes?

04:22.680 --> 04:23.970
Well, I could do git stash apply

04:23.970 --> 04:26.280
but I'm just gonna pop off the stash.

04:26.280 --> 04:28.620
As I talked about in the section

04:28.620 --> 04:30.150
or the videos prior to this.

04:30.150 --> 04:33.240
I usually just use git stash and git stash pop.

04:33.240 --> 04:37.050
So git stash pop will then retrieve the changes,

04:37.050 --> 04:38.610
right, that I stashed away.

04:38.610 --> 04:42.570
And now I can keep working or I can add and commit.

04:42.570 --> 04:44.430
I'll just add and commit.

04:44.430 --> 04:49.430
Git commit -m, add the truth, and we're done.

04:50.010 --> 04:53.160
All right, so I can switch back to master.

04:53.160 --> 04:54.840
Switch to the truth.

04:54.840 --> 04:56.010
It's not part of the exercise

04:56.010 --> 04:58.890
but we just stashed something in the The stash.

04:58.890 --> 04:59.910
Nothing crazy.

04:59.910 --> 05:01.890
I hope you're able to get through that

05:01.890 --> 05:03.780
and I hope you don't actually hate your boss.

05:03.780 --> 05:04.683
Okay, bye.
